=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough investigation of the reported fault — PC15 unable to reach PC16 — found no anomaly anywhere in the relevant path. Both endpoints (pc15 at 172.18.51.15/24 and pc16 at 172.18.51.16/24) are correctly addressed on the same subnet, with their eth0 interfaces up and LOWER_UP. They both connect to switch10, which presents a single flat bridge (br0) encompassing all nine access ports and the uplink to mswitch2 — there is no VLAN separation, no STP blocking, and no port isolation of any kind. Direct ICMP connectivity was confirmed in both directions: pc15→pc16 returned 4/4 packets with sub-1 ms latency, and pc16→pc15 returned 4/4 packets with ~0.44 ms latency. Neither host has any iptables rules installed (all chains are ACCEPT-policy with zero entries), and both have a correct default gateway of 172.18.51.254. The switch10 bridge table and the mswitch2 uplink port are all operational. There is no injected fault, misconfiguration, ACL, or L2 isolation condition affecting the PC15–PC16 segment. The network is operating normally; the reported symptom is not reproducible and does not correspond to any present network fault. The user should verify host-level software (file-sharing service, Windows Firewall, SMB configuration) rather than the network infrastructure.
=== END ===